LanguageData.RimTalk.Settings.AdvancedHelpContent:
Advanced Preset Guide
Advanced mode builds the prompt from a list of entries. The list order is the message order unless you use InChat.
Key concepts: 1. Order: Entries are sent in list order. There is no fixed system/user/assistant sequence. 2. Role: Each entry can be System, User, or Assistant. 3. Position: - Relative: Follows list order. - InChat: Inserts into chat history. - Depth 0: After the most recent message. - Depth 5: 5 messages back into the past. 4. History marker: The entry marked as main history inserts {{chat.history}} at that spot. 5. Defaults worth keeping: {{json.format}}, {{context}}, {{prompt}}. 6. Custom Role: If set, the entry is sent as a User message and prefixed with [role: your_role].
Scriban Magic (Dynamic Content) Use double braces {{ ... }} to insert real-time game data.
Advanced Context: - Initiator: {{ pawn.LabelShort }} (The pawn speaking) - Recipient: {{ recipient.LabelShort }} (The pawn being spoken to) - All Participants: {{ for p in pawns }}{{ p.LabelShort }}, {{ end }}
Advanced Examples: - Getting All Colonists: {{ for p in PawnsFinder.AllMaps_FreeColonists }} * {{ p.LabelShort }} is {{ p.job }}{{ end }}
- Getting Last 3 Quests: {{ for q in Find.QuestManager.QuestsListForReading | array.limit 3 }} - {{ q.name }}: {{ q.description | Sanitize }}{{ end }}
- Map Environment: The weather is {{ map.weather }} and it is {{ map.temperature }}°C.
- Pawn Needs: {{ for need in pawn.needs.AllNeeds }} * {{ need.def.label }}: {{ need.CurLevelPercentage }}{{ end }}
- Check Status: {{ if IsInCombat pawn }}You are currently in a fight!{{ end }}
- Complex Logic Example: {{ if recipient != null }} You are talking to {{ recipient.LabelShort }}. {{ if recipient.Dead }}...but they are dead.{{ end }} {{ else }} You are thinking to yourself. {{ end }}
Crucial Tips: - Case Sensitivity: Functions are strict. Use GetRole, not getrole. - Reference Preview: Use the dedicated tab to see every property you can use! - JSON: The {{json.format}} variable is vital for AI logic. Only override it manually in System entries if you are an experienced user.
